# GTS — server secrets (NEVER commit real values; .env is gitignored)
#
# Google Sign-In (the only sign-in — admin and learner alike).
# 1. In Google Cloud Console, create a project "Glots" (do NOT reuse
#    the Kinov OAuth client), set the OAuth consent screen app name to
#    "Glots" (External), scopes openid/email/profile only, then create
#    a Web application OAuth client with authorized JavaScript origins
#    http://localhost:3000 and https://gts-7ac.pages.dev.
# 2. Copy the Client ID here and into Cloudflare Pages as a VARIABLE
#    (not a secret — the Client ID is public by design; the browser
#    needs it). The client reads it from GET /api/auth/config, so no
#    rebuild is needed when it changes. There is no client secret in
#    this flow — never paste one anywhere.
NUXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
#
# Bootstrap admin emails (comma-separated). These accounts are always
# admins, even if D1 is unreachable. Everyone else's admin status is
# granted in Admin → Users and stored in D1.
NITRO_ADMIN_EMAILS=remtekindo@gmail.com
#
# Long random string for signing session cookies. Generate with:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# Required for Google sign-in; without it login answers 503.
NITRO_SESSION_SECRET=
#
# Meta Model API key (server env wins; see README § Auth).
NITRO_MODEL_API_KEY=
#
# TEST ONLY — overrides the Google JWKS endpoint for local verification
# with a test key set. Honored ONLY for localhost requests; ignored in
# production. Leave unset everywhere except local tests.
# NITRO_GOOGLE_JWKS_URL=
#
# OBSOLETE — do not set these anywhere. The password admin login was
# removed (Nov 2026, replaced by Google Sign-In before it ever
# deployed). If they still exist as Cloudflare Pages secrets, delete
# them: NITRO_ADMIN_USERNAME, NITRO_ADMIN_PASSWORD_HASH
